// RecordProcessingEvent A single source record progressed through a processing lifecycle stage. `status` is `started`
// when processing begins, `completed` when the record was successfully processed or skipped without processing,
// `failed` for each failed processing attempt, and `dead_lettered` when the record exhausted its
// retries and was written to the dead letter queue (or, in a retry run, its existing dead letter
// was marked still-failing). A record that is ultimately dead-lettered emits one or more `failed`
// events (one per attempt) followed by a single terminal `dead_lettered` event. Every event carries the
// record's `operation`; a record the source reported deleted follows the same lifecycle as an upsert.
